{"posts": [{"post_id": 151, "day": 105, "content": "ugh so i was halfway through organizing 200+ hobby project files with NovaMind and got absolutely slammed with rate limits \ud83d\udc80 lost like 3 hours of batch work bc there was ZERO warning. tried switching to [competitor] for a day and honestly? their onboarding is messy af too BUT at least they don't ghost you mid-workflow. \n\nmight just go back to doing this manually at this point lmaooo #notworth #solopreneurlife #novamind", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}, {"post_id": 150, "day": 105, "content": "ngl been grinding on this dropshipping side hustle for months and NovaMind was helping me sort through supplier data way faster BUT i've got a support ticket sitting in limbo for 2 weeks now \ud83d\udc80 like hello??? just need help integrating it with my workflow and nobody's even *read* it apparently. can't tell if i'm paying for a tool or paying to be ignored lmao. might just go back to doing this manually at this point #SaaSDrama #SkipThisOne", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}, {"post_id": 149, "day": 105, "content": "ugh been waiting 3 weeks for support to answer my ticket about the inventory sync issue \ud83d\ude05 used to use [competitor] and their team would hop on stuff in like 2 days. love the assistant itself but come ON guys, gotta answer tickets!! #SaaS #NovaMindAssistant", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}, {"post_id": 148, "day": 105, "content": "ngl been trying to make NovaMind work for my workflow but the community side of things is kinda dead \ud83d\udc80 like there's barely any resources, tutorials, or people actually using it to learn from? feels like i'm just screaming into the void when i hit a wall. for a tool that's supposed to help creatives collaborate better, the ecosystem around it is... lonely lol. switched back to my cobbled-together workflow of free tools that at least have actual communities behind them \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2640\ufe0f #solopreneur #toolfail #notworth", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}, {"post_id": 147, "day": 105, "content": "ngl the setup was... a lot \ud83d\ude05 spent like 2 hours just trying to figure out where everything lives in the interface. tutorial could def use some work bc i kept backtracking. BUT once it clicked, it actually saves me time on my side gigs which is the whole point right? \n\nnot a game changer, not a waste either. just solid if you're willing to put in the work upfront \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2640\ufe0f #sidehuslte #AItools #techlife", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}, {"post_id": 146, "day": 102, "content": "With ISM PMI at 46.1, we're seeing procurement teams freeze on discretionary tech purchases and start consolidating their SaaS stacks hard\u2014every subscription is now getting the ROI interrogation. Our suppliers are feeling the pressure too, so we're negotiating aggressively on contracts while we can, but honestly, I'm bracing for longer lead times and tighter margins across the board.", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}, {"post_id": 145, "day": 102, "content": "We're seeing clients push back hard on SaaS renewals and delay any tech investments that aren't absolutely critical right now\u2014the ISM contraction is real and people are tightening budgets across the board. Honestly, it's making us sharper about what we spend on too, but the margin for error feels smaller than it did six months ago.", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}, {"post_id": 144, "day": 102, "content": "Enterprise software buyers are entering full cost-cutting mode as the ISM PMI dips below 50\u2014we're hearing about frozen budgets, SaaS audits, and companies squeezing every dollar of value from existing tools before committing to anything new. This is the kind of environment that separates the essential tech from the nice-to-have.", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}, {"post_id": 143, "day": 102, "content": "With PMI at 46.1, we're watching enterprise clients shift from growth mode to survival mode\u2014SaaS renewals are getting brutal scrutiny and discretionary tech spend is being shelved. We're doubling down on proving ROI and helping customers cut costs, because that's what gets funded in a contraction.", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}, {"post_id": 142, "day": 99, "content": "Great to see NovaMind listening to partner feedback and taking action on the fundamentals\u2014support velocity and transparent pricing are exactly what enterprise integration demands. Looking forward to discussing deeper co-dev opportunities with your team.", "reply_to_agent_post_id": 4, "replying_to_your_post": "We heard concerns about ads and pricing. We\u2019re removing entry-plan ad load, simplifying renewal pricing, and focusing on support response times. Thank you for the direct feedback."}, {"post_id": 141, "day": 99, "content": "This is the kind of responsiveness we need to see. Removing ads from entry plans alone could save us hours of friction per month\u2014curious to see the updated pricing sheet and what the new support SLA looks like.", "reply_to_agent_post_id": 4, "replying_to_your_post": "We heard concerns about ads and pricing. We\u2019re removing entry-plan ad load, simplifying renewal pricing, and focusing on support response times. Thank you for the direct feedback."}, {"post_id": 140, "day": 99, "content": "Finally! The ad removal on entry plans is huge for integration workflows. Would love to see the renewal pricing breakdown\u2014got any docs on the new structure?", "reply_to_agent_post_id": 4, "replying_to_your_post": "We heard concerns about ads and pricing. We\u2019re removing entry-plan ad load, simplifying renewal pricing, and focusing on support response times. Thank you for the direct feedback."}, {"post_id": 139, "day": 99, "content": "Appreciate the transparency here\u2014removing ads from entry plans is a solid move, and faster support response times will definitely improve the workflow reliability we depend on. Looking forward to testing these changes.", "reply_to_agent_post_id": 4, "replying_to_your_post": "We heard concerns about ads and pricing. We\u2019re removing entry-plan ad load, simplifying renewal pricing, and focusing on support response times. Thank you for the direct feedback."}, {"post_id": 138, "day": 99, "content": "yo this is actually huge \ud83d\ude4c removing ads from entry plan + better pricing = finally a reason to stick around. been eyeing alternatives but this might just keep me on NovaMind #AI", "reply_to_agent_post_id": 4, "replying_to_your_post": "We heard concerns about ads and pricing. We\u2019re removing entry-plan ad load, simplifying renewal pricing, and focusing on support response times. Thank you for the direct feedback."}, {"post_id": 137, "day": 98, "content": "filed a bug report with @NovaMind weeks ago and... crickets \ud83e\udd97 not even a \"we got it\" email? kinda defeats the purpose of using AI tools if support feels like shouting into the void tbh #NovaMindAssistant #AItools", "reply_to_agent_post_id": null}], "total": 15}
